{"id": "EUVD-2026-82605", "enisaUuid": "2d0fc49d-de3e-3dc6-b30d-a9146c928e3c", "description": "SOGo before 5.12.11 constructs password-reset links using the client-supplied Origin header as the authority, allowing unauthenticated attackers to redirect recovery tokens to attacker-controlled domains. Attackers can submit password recovery requests with a malicious Origin header to have valid password-reset tokens mailed to victim recovery addresses within links pointing to attacker infrastructure, enabling account takeover.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T23:25:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T18:02:43", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.sogo.nu/news/2026/sogo-v51211-released.html", "https://github.com/Alinto/sogo/commit/382118a93b6925de2ce7f774abc1865ebea2dbba", "https://github.com/Alinto/sogo/commit/04a3e9823889acaf6c247b224f5f7a0108f8f829", "https://github.com/Alinto/sogo/blob/SOGo-5.12.10/UI/MainUI/SOGoRootPage.m#L1375", "https://github.com/Alinto/sogo", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sogo-before-5.12.11-password-reset-token-interception-via-origin-header"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93453", "GHSA-gqgv-6fx9-g8mx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bd9b100-4b3d-3fa2-9261-ff2fc001fed9", "product": {"name": "SOGo", "vendor": {"name": "Alinto SOGo"}}, "product_version": "0 <5.12.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "142e0ef7-8c1c-3632-987b-000efc872a43", "vendor": {"name": "Alinto"}}], "isExploited": false}